  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CIJV &amp; PBHJV WTLDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project targets priority wetlands and associated uplands in areas of the Pacific Habitat Bird Joint Venture (PHBJV) and the Canadian Intermountain Joint Venture (CIJV)located within the province of British Columbia. Project activities will permanently protect 386acres through fee simple acquisition, enhance 489 acres, and manage 19,665 acres of critical habitat for many priority species including Red Necked and Eared Grebe, Brant, Surf Scoter,Greater Scaup, Mallard, Cinnamon Teal, Northern Pintail, Blue-winged Teal, American Wigeon,Barrows Goldeneye, Oystercatcher, Great Blue Heron, Northern Shoveler, Bald Eagle, Trumpeter Swan, Harlequin Duck, Black-necked Stilt, Spotted Sandpiper, and Killdeer.</narrative>
  </description>
